<newsitem itemid="633801" id="root" date="1997-06-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>MALAYSIA: Berjaya Capital year net profit higher.</title>
<headline>Berjaya Capital year net profit higher.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended April 30, 1997</p>
<p>			  (in million ringgit unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 166.40	   vs	  108.31</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	 30.0	    vs	   19.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  831.99	    vs	  624.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  276.64	    vs	  174.54</p>
<p>    Minorities  less	 35.92	    vs   less  19.76</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  21.09	    vs	    1.38</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)     23.0	     vs	   11.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Berjaya Capital Bhd is involved in insurance, hire-purchase and leasing. The extraordinary items mainly comprise a gain arising from disposal of quoted investments.</p>
</text>
